/aveloxis

# Sphinx moves the previous .buildinfo here on a config-change rebuild; the live
# .buildinfo is tracked, the backup is build noise (PR #197 round 15).
docs/_build/html/.buildinfo.bak

# Sphinx's cache: environment.pickle and one .doctree per page, Python pickles.
# sphinx-build without -E loads them, and unpickling runs the callables a file
# names, so a tracked one is code a pull request can ship unseen; they also
# embed the builder's checkout path. The site needs none of them. Python
# bytecode is the same class: every docs build imports docs/_ext, and an import
# reads a __pycache__ .pyc even under sys.dont_write_bytecode (0.29.144,
# TestNoTrackedCodeOnLoadCaches). sphinx-build -M writes its cache to
# docs/_build/doctrees/; a native extension module under docs/ is imported
# before the .py of its name, replacing the reviewed source (*.so and *.dylib
# are ignored above with the other binaries; *.pyd is Windows').
docs/_build/html/.doctrees/
docs/_build/doctrees/
*.pickle
*.doctree
__pycache__/
*.py[co]
*.pyd

